        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{|x|}{x}=\\begin{cases}1,&x>0,\\\\-1,&x<0.\\end{cases}$",
          "worked": "For $x>0$,\n$$\\frac{|x|}{x}=\\frac{x}{x}=1.$$\nFor $x<0$,\n$$\\frac{|x|}{x}=\\frac{-x}{x}=-1.$$\nAt $x=0$ the denominator is zero, so the function is undefined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
